○ ob-o4g · DECISION/ADR: layer-to-engine assignment across NPU, GPU, and CPU   [● P1 · OPEN]
Type: decision
Created: 2026-08-02 · Updated: 2026-08-02

DESCRIPTION

  Fix the partitioning with measurements behind it. WORKING HYPOTHESIS as of  
  2026-08-02 (PLAN.md 3.1), to be confirmed or refuted rather than assumed:   
  Armv9.2 CPU hosts the 24 GDN linear layers (sequential scan, bandwidth-bound
  at decode, recurrent state stays resident), while the 8 full-attention      
  layers and dense FFN blocks go to GPU and/or NPU (large dense matmuls).     
                                                                              
  Note this is the reverse of the naive 'offload everything to the NPU'       
  framing, and it is deliberate: on the CIX P1 the Cortex-A720/A520 cores and 
  the Immortalis G720 GPU are both Arm IP while the NPU is the only non-Arm   
  engine, so CPU+GPU work is what the competition's 40-point Arm-specific     
  optimization criterion actually rewards.                                    
                                                                              
  Must account for boundary-crossing cost (bead ob-t3b.3): 16 crossings per   
  token in a 3:1 stack, latency-dominated rather than bandwidth-dominated.    
  Expect the outcome to be a PHASE-DEPENDENT mapping - NPU earning its place  
  in prefill where matmuls amortize dispatch, decode possibly staying entirely
  on CPU/GPU - rather than one static assignment. Record whichever way the    
  measurements fall.                                                          



LABELS: hardware

PARENT
